From 50bc7a364fa7c7db1a2fef5f83cc3a1913ca53cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KiralyCraft <alexucu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:20:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] present: disarm the wait-fence callback before
 re-execution

A fence notification is one-shot, but re_execute() can leave the Present
request alive while it waits for its target MSC. Clear the callback before
re-entering the execution path. If that path must wait again, it installs
a new callback itself.

This is required when the Sync trigger walker restarts after a callback:
otherwise a still-live request can be called repeatedly in the same scan.
It also prevents a later trigger of a reused fence from executing the old
request again.

The same callback-lifetime correction is used by Termux:X11:
https://github.com/KiralyCraft/termux-x11/commit/fc534e514d7ad4851d0aca3357495816260e4549

This patch is from https://github.com/lfdevs/xwayland/pull/2.
---
 present/present_execute.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/present/present_execute.c b/present/present_execute.c
index 5253344a1..9e11a3473 100644
--- a/present/present_execute.c
+++ b/present/present_execute.c
@@ -38,6 +38,10 @@ present_wait_fence_triggered(void *param)
     ScreenPtr               screen = vblank->screen;
     present_screen_priv_ptr screen_priv = present_screen_priv(screen);
 
+    /* Re-execution may keep this request alive until its target MSC.
+     * Disarm this notification; a new wait will install a new callback. */
+    present_fence_set_callback(vblank->wait_fence, NULL, NULL);
+
     screen_priv->re_execute(vblank);
 }
 
